course: dictionary
lesson: 11317
title: Yet, three jobs in one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The small word yet has three jobs, and the words around it show you which one. Ask yourself: is it about time, is it a "but", or is it "even more"?
explain: First, yet can mean up to now: «Have you finished yet?» The answer «Not yet» means it has not happened so far, but it may still happen. Yet often sits at the end of a question or a negative sentence.
explain: Second, yet can mean but or still, joining two ideas that seem to pull against each other: «It was cold, yet sunny.» Third, yet can mean even or still more: «yet another cake» means one more cake on top of the ones already there.
fact: Yet can mean up to now, as in «Are we there yet?» and «Not yet!».
fact: «As yet» and «not yet» both mean it has not happened so far.
fact: Yet can mean but or still, joining two ideas: «It was cold, yet sunny.»
fact: Yet can mean even or still more, as in «yet another».
fact: A growth mindset phrase is «I can't do it yet», which means you may learn it later.
exercise: «Have you finished yet?» What does yet mean here? | But, joining two ideas | Even more, one extra | Very loudly | *Up to now, so far
exercise: «It was cold, yet sunny.» Which word could replace yet here? | Up to now | Quickly | Loudly | *But
exercise: «yet another cake» means one more cake on top of the others. What does yet mean in this phrase? | But, still | *Even more, one extra | Up to now | Not finished
test: «The Indus writing has not yet been understood.» What does yet mean? | Very loudly | *Up to now, so far | Even more | But
test: «Radiation hurts animals, yet people being gone helps them.» What does yet mean? | Up to now | Quickly | Even more | *But, still
exam: Jayden says «I can't do it yet» is a growth mindset phrase. What does yet suggest? | It means you can never do it | It means you already did it | *It means you cannot do it so far, but you may learn | It means you are not trying
